course: dictionary
lesson: 56
title: Accuser and accused
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An accuser is a person who says that someone else has done something wrong or committed a crime. The verb is accuse: to accuse someone is to say they did wrong. Look at the clues around the word to find out who is doing the accusing.
explain: «Innocent until proven guilty» means the person accused does not have to prove they are innocent: the accusers must prove they are guilty. So the job of proving the case belongs to the accuser, not the accused.
explain: In a courtroom, the accuser faces the accused, the person who is blamed. A fair trial lets both sides speak, so each can tell their side of the story.
explain: In the Bible, «the accuser» is a name for Satan, who accuses people before God. This is a special use of the word, so check the context to see whether a story is about a court or about the Bible.
fact: An accuser is a person who says that someone else has done something wrong or committed a crime.
fact: The accused is the person who is blamed for doing something wrong.
fact: «The accuser» is also a name for Satan in the Bible, who accuses people before God.
fact: «Face your accuser» means to stand up to the person who has blamed you.
fact: The idea that the accuser must prove the case comes from Roman law and is in the 1948 Universal Declaration of Human Rights.
exercise: «The accuser told the judge that the man had stolen the bike.» Who is the accuser? | *The person who said the man stole the bike | The judge | The bike | The man who was blamed
exercise: «Innocent until proven guilty» means who must prove something? | The accused, who must prove they are innocent | Nobody has to prove anything | *The accusers, who must prove the person is guilty | The judge alone
exercise: «The accuser and the accused stood in the court.» Find and copy the word that means the person who is blamed. | stood | court | accuser | *accused
test: Which word means the person who says someone did wrong? | witness | *accuser | verdict | judge
test: In the Bible, what does «the accuser» mean? | A kind of bird | A king of Rome | *A name for Satan, who accuses people before God | A famous judge
exam: In «Innocent until proven guilty», who must prove the case? | the judge's clerk | *the accusers | the accused | no one
